WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.040
Trial Review Desk helps clinical research coordinators
review possible cancer trial matches.

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:17.240
It brings the evidence, follow-up, and the reason for
each decision into one workspace.

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:22.240
Each row pairs a fictional patient with a trial
protocol.

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:31.080
The queue shows upcoming visits, review progress, and
who owns each case.

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:35.600
Case one is waiting on a single test result.

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:41.720
The watchlist shows the owner and the event that brings
the case back.

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:48.400
When a fictional report arrives, the coordinator
rechecks the evidence.

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:54.920
The follow-up stays open until it is resolved.

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:58.760
Case five shows a confirmed exclusion.

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:03.840
The handoff stays blocked even when the inclusion checks
pass.

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:10.400
A structured reason explains why the match was closed.

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:16.720
In case seven, the simulated AI suggestion relies on an
older note.

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:20.080
The evidence panel shows both dated excerpts.

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:28.760
The current note supports a different answer for this
fictional criterion.

00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:37.360
The coordinator selects Override, cites the current
note, and tags the error as an outdated note.

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:45.920
After saving, the case shows who changed the suggestion,
when, and why.

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:52.600
The AI Evaluation Inspector keeps the original
prediction and the correction visible.

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:59.680
It counts suggestions reviewed, unique suggestions
overridden, and total override actions.

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:05.920
The benchmark uses a fixed set of fictional examples.

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:10.480
The same Inspector entry opens a short visit brief.

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:16.280
It shows reviewed evidence, the open question, and the
next step.

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:22.480
Selecting the citation opens the original excerpt.

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:29.840
Analytics shows how reviews progress and which protocol
checks block cases.

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:45.000
The goal is a clear next step for every possible match,
with evidence and a reason the team can trace.
